From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: win32u, dwmapi: the Rounded style rounds windows' corners

David asked for a look like newer Windows beside the Windows 10 one, each
part choosable. Its most visible mark is round window corners. With
HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Style "Rounded" = 1 (Settings >
Personalization > Colors), every top-level window with a title bar gets
8 px rounded corners (scaled with its DPI):

- win32u: the rounding is the window surface's shape (the path a window
  region takes to X), never a window region -- GetWindowRgn and hit-testing
  are unchanged. Square corners stay while maximized or minimized, for
  layered windows (they draw their own edges), and when the program has a
  region of its own. The style is read at most twice a second per process,
  so turning it on or off reaches a window at its next move, size or frame
  change (Settings' change of style repaints every frame).
- dwmapi: DWMWA_WINDOW_CORNER_PREFERENCE is honoured -- DONOTROUND keeps a
  window square, ROUNDSMALL rounds by 4 px -- and read back by
  DwmGetWindowAttribute. It is recorded as a window property win32u reads.

Gate: test/rounded-gate.sh (read off the screen, over a green desktop).
